BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to 3D Design with TinkerCAD
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T190000
UID:6ab1990aab7a8e0037c37081@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of 3D design with Tinkercad - a free web app 
 for everyone. By combining simple shapes\, it is possible to create comple
 x designs and potentially\, 3D print the result with ease. In this class\,
  participants will create a custom pumpkin keychain that will be 3D print
 ed and available for pick-up before Halloween. All ages are welcome\, basi
 c keyboard and mouse skills are required.\nRegistration is required.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 2nd Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab1990aab7a8e0037c37081
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
