UID:6aadd74ef9ed2e003851d204@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us   for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and 
 discuss nine real and   replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on works
 hop. Participants   will be entertained and educated\, not just about the 
 fossils themselves\, but   the palaeontological aspects that underpin them
 . Concepts include evolution\,   fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (p
 hylogeny) and — of course — dinosaurs!\n*Registration will open two we
 eks before.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aadd74ef9ed2e003851d204
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
