UID:6a88a6614cb69d003e2261e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages 6-12.\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for 
 participants 10mins before the program starts. Ingredient lists will be av
 ailable. Snacks are generously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nSeptember
  the PopUpLearningLab will be visiting S. Walter Stewart branch!\nSeptembe
 r 15 - 3D Printing\nSeptember 22 - Makey Makey\nSeptember 29 - Snap Circui
 ts (including the Snap Circuits rover)
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88a6614cb69d003e2261e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T170000
UID:6a90a7624cb69d003e23de0c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages 6-12.\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for 
 participants are free of the top 10 priority allergens in Canada: peanuts
 \, tree nuts\, milk\, eggs\, seafood\, soy\, wheat\, sesame seeds\, mustar
 d and sulphites. ​Ingredient lists will be available.\nSnacks are genero
 usly supported\, in part\, by donors.\nIf you or your child lives with a d
 isability\, and requires an accessibility accommodation to participate in 
 this program\, please contact Accessibility Service by email\naccessiblese
 rvices@tpl.ca\nor voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. Please con
 tact at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90a7624cb69d003e23de0c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
