BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T170000
UID:6aa98abca433d308573ba64a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun!\nFor ages 6-12 years old.\nSnacks are offered during the After Schoo
 l Club for participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are ge
 nerously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nMonday\, October 5:\nDigest Thi
 s! Biogas workshop with\nRelay Education\nIn this interactive & educationa
 l workshop\, in honour of\nScience Literacy Week\n\,\nparticipants will di
 scover & learn:\nhow the digestion of organic waste is used as a form of 
 renewable energy\nhow biogas can help reduce our impact on the environment
 \nunderstand how a biodigester's breakdown of organic waste & the release
  of gas is like the process of human digestion\nmix some simple household 
 chemicals together to observe their reactions\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa98abca433d308573ba64a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
