BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Design Your Own Tote Bag
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T170000
UID:6ab59f08a5dbde002aa70575@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the art of block printing and textile design to create
  your own custom tote bag – and take it with you for trick-or-treating! 
 Budding artists will learn how patterns\, symbols\, and shapes are used in
  cultures around the world before designing and printing their own unique 
 creations onto a reusable canvas tote bag\, using stamps\, blocks\, fabric
  paints\, stencils and decorative elements.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab59f08a5dbde002aa70575
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
