SUMMARY:Paint a Mini Worry Monster
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T170000
UID:6a90590929a7dd0d67470b69@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Paint your own mini worry monster on stone. Squeezing and rubb
 ing the stone can be soothing and help ease your worries.\nFor children ag
 es 6-12.\nRegistration is required. Register by visiting Tpl.ca.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Rm 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90590929a7dd0d67470b69
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIGITAL LITERACY: 2 Truths & a Lie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T170000
UID:6aa1c4a28cf597003f925f43@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to tell news from fake news. Try some quizzes\, and then
  come up with your own fake news headline and see if you can fool anyone. 
 Participants will pair up on iPads to find real news headlines to include 
 their fake headline with. Registration is required.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room BC (Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa1c4a28cf597003f925f43
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hands on Henna with Hina Yasir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T180000
UID:6ab2ed1065abe8002a7b5404@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Islamic Heritage Month with Henna!\nDiscover the art
  of henna\, decorative designs which are created on a person's body\, usin
 g\na paste of natural organic henna.  Observe and enjoy the henna\napplica
 tion and learn about its history\, recipe and traditions.  Led by Henna Ar
 tist\, Hina Yasir. All ages welcome.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2ed1065abe8002a7b5404
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T190000
UID:6ab6fc978cf597003f96825b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nNote: Customers are no 
 longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to using a 3
 D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This 
 class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D printing a
 nd how to use the Prusa software.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, LC2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6fc978cf597003f96825b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
